<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Peter III of Russia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1728">1728</a>–<a href="/years/1762">1762</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Peter III was emperor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a> for six months in 1762, a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peter-the-great">Peter the Great</a> raised in Holstein. In 1745 he married Sophie of Anhalt-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zerbst">Zerbst</a>, who took the name Catherine. His abrupt peace with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> and unpopular policies led to a coup in which Catherine seized the throne as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catherine-the-great">Catherine II</a>, and he was killed soon after.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/peter-iii-of-russia.jpg" alt="Peter III of Russia" width="320" height="418" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lucas Conrad Pfandzelt · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Coronation_portrait_of_Peter_III_of_Russia_-1761.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
